seg-a4d279582461 = Field guide: a real receiver on a site

# text
seg-55ea4b46bb44 = These steps take one receiver from its box to an unattended Station on Linux. They use only the open engine. The Station reads; it never configures a receiver, so step { "1" } uses the maker's own tool.

# text
seg-4e0ea401b12e = { "1" }. Make the receiver send what the Station reads

# text
seg-be7af5378360 = Set the receiver's output with its maker's tool (u-blox u-center, Septentrio's web interface or RxTools, and so on), and save that configuration in the receiver so it survives a power cycle.

