seg-d7fe35052aa8 = { "6" }. Day to day

# text
# c1: /status
seg-76e9cbabb828 = <b>Gaps.</b> A source with no input is counted as a gap (<c1/>, per source), never filled. Each reconnection starts a new file.

# text
seg-cc16cced7827 = <b>Time.</b> Epoch times in the files come from the receiver's own messages, not from the computer's clock.

# text
# c1: [http]
# c2: token_file
seg-777a474ea7e7 = <b>Off the site.</b> Keep the status port local. To read it from elsewhere, give <c1/> a <c2/> and put a TLS tunnel in front, as for the fleet report.

